# Cursor Rules for SaniLine Security Compliance

Always adhere to military-grade code security standards using SaniLine:
1. When generating code lines or editing files, ensure no hardcoded secrets (AWS, GitHub, OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Stripe, Supabase), shell=True invocations, child_process.exec shell calls, Prototype Pollution (__proto__), DOM XSS (dangerouslySetInnerHTML), Trojan Source Unicode overrides (CVE-2021-42574), or insecure deserialization are introduced.
2. You may execute `saniline check <file> --compact` or `npx saniline check <file> --compact` to verify and auto-patch your modifications.
3. Use `result.to_token_compact()` (Python) or `result.toTokenCompact()` (JS) when calling SaniLine or via MCP (`saniline mcp`, `npx -y saniline mcp`) to minimize context token usage (<10 tokens).
